                        "recommendationid": "237873481",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198101233182",
                            "num_reviews": 168,
                            "playtime_forever": 1290,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1290,
                            "last_played": 1792173591
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is the perfect game to play with friends… until a certain point.\n\nYou jump into a session, complete everything in one region, and move on to the next. The problem is that the gameplay starts to feel like the same loop over and over again. The difficulty doesn’t really seem to evolve beyond throwing more enemies at you, which also means more and more helicopters.\n\nAt some point, I just didn’t feel like the game was respecting my time. We couldn’t even finish it because the repetition eventually became too much. It’s genuinely fun for the first few hours, especially when playing with friends, but it starts to lose its charm after that.\n\nI do enjoy Ubisoft games, but this feels like another example of the same formula they’ve been using for years. It’s essentially the Assassin’s Creed formula applied to another game: fun at first, but eventually you start noticing how repetitive everything becomes.\n\nI had a good time with the first few hours, but unfortunately, that wasn’t enough to keep me playing until the end.",
